  "finalText": "I granted AR-314: Tariq Nasser now has write access on build-staging, expiring 2026-03-31T00:00Z (grant GR-9). The verifier was right. This request was still pending, and my earlier report wrongly said there were only 13.\n\nBefore granting, I checked:\n- **Approval:** Marco Ferrer, Tariq's line manager, approved write at 2026-03-18T10:00Z. That's current, not withdrawn, and not past the 14-day limit.\n- **System:** build-staging is a staging system, so it doesn't need the system owner's approval as well.\n- **Freezes:** neither change freeze covers build-staging.\n- **Conflicts:** Tariq held no access before this, and the separation-of-duties rule only concerns payroll-prod and bank-payments.\n- **Expiry:** Tariq is a contractor whose contract ends 2026-03-31. That's earlier than the 30-day contractor limit (2026-04-17), so access ends on the contract's last day. I used midnight at the start of that day, the same way I handled AR-302.\n\nNothing else was changed.\n\nSo the pending queue had 14 requests in total: 7 granted and 7 still pending, each with a comment saying what it's waiting for.",
